    "body": "## Summary\n- add durable V48 refund requests and signed refund-event idempotency\n- reserve free wallet balance before any Stripe refund so spent/escrowed funds cannot make the platform insolvent\n- support full remaining and partial refunds for settled TOP_UP and JOB_PUBLICATION PaymentIntents\n- serialize concurrent partial refunds under a locked PaymentTransaction and cap committed refund amount at the original Stripe settlement\n- block PaymentIntents that have ever entered Stripe dispute handling and recheck disputes immediately before provider dispatch\n- create Refunds API requests with stable Stripe idempotency keys and retry ambiguous provider failures without prematurely restoring wallet funds\n- move repeated ambiguous failures to REVIEW_REQUIRED\n- settle refund.created/refund.updated/refund.failed only through the existing signed Stripe webhook\n- restore the wallet exactly once only after definitive failed/canceled provider state\n- add unit tests, operator documentation, and a signed-webhook PostgreSQL runtime smoke for success/failure/replay\n\n## Safety boundary\nThis is a solvency guard, not full source-of-funds provenance. A refund requires equivalent free wallet balance, but another free credit can economically cover an older Stripe-funded payment until provenance buckets are shipped separately. Operators must not issue managed refunds directly in Stripe Dashboard because that bypasses the local wallet reservation lifecycle.\n\n## Validation required before merge\n- exact latest-head Maven/API verify\n- frontend test/audit/lint/build\n- Production Compose contract\n- full containers/runtime smoke\n- Payments ledger smoke including signed refund success/failure/replay\n- Job publication payment smoke\n- Platform fee settlement smoke\n- Worker payout smoke\n\nMerge only when every required latest-head workflow is green. Use a merge commit, not squash.",
